course: dictionary
lesson: 8569
title: Scavengers: nature's clean-up crew
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A scavenger is an animal, or sometimes a person, that finds food or useful things that someone else has left behind. «Vultures are scavengers» tells you that vultures do not usually hunt. They feed on animals that are already dead.
explain: Look at the words around it to check. «A predator hunts and kills other animals for food; scavengers eat animals that are already dead.» Predator and scavenger are set against each other, so the clues show that a scavenger does not kill its own food.
explain: The word has two other uses. A scavenger can be a person who searches through rubbish for things to use or sell. A scavenger hunt is a game in which you search for a list of things. Swap each meaning into the sentence to see which one fits.
fact: A scavenger is an animal that feeds on dead animals or scraps left by other creatures.
fact: A scavenger can also be a person who searches through rubbish for things to use or sell.
fact: A scavenger hunt is a game in which you search for a list of things.
fact: Vultures, hyenas and crabs are examples of scavengers.
fact: Scavengers help clean up nature by eating dead bodies, so they are sometimes called nature's clean-up crew.
exercise: «Vultures are scavengers whose very strong stomach acid kills most germs from rotting meat.» What do vultures mainly eat? | *Animals that are already dead | Other vultures | Plants and seeds | Live fish from the river
exercise: «A predator hunts and kills other animals for food; scavengers eat animals that are already dead.» Which word tells you a scavenger eats what is already dead? | *scavengers | predator | hunts | food
exercise: At the party, the children played a scavenger hunt. What is a scavenger hunt? | A kind of rubbish bin | A trip to the zoo | *A game where you search for a list of things | A race to see who can run fastest
test: «Real piranhas are mostly timid shoaling fish and scavengers.» What does scavengers mean here? | *Animals that eat things already dead | Teeth that tear meat | Fish that hunt the biggest animals | Fast swimmers
test: Which word means a person who searches through rubbish for things to use or sell? | Shoal | Prey | *Scavenger | Predator
exam: «When vultures nearly died out in India, carcasses lay uncleaned and disease spread.» Why did disease spread? | Because the carcasses were too small to see | Because vultures ate too many live cattle | Because the rain washed the germs away | *Because the scavengers that clean up dead bodies had nearly gone
